I've written two task files and the issue responses and committed them as f84dc0ef. Git ignores session_plan/, so the commit needed git add -f. Nothing is implemented yet, as planned.

Task 1 (evolve, the DREAM milestone): `yoyo risk accuracy` should show each event's recorded unhittable and unmeasurable counts next to its percentage.
• Most of this milestone has already landed. The watch, ci_harvest and CLI writers already record unhittable_surprises and unmeasurable_surprises in .yoyo/risk_validations.jsonl.
• The part still missing is the display. When I ran yoyo risk accuracy, the "Recent Validation Events" list printed 0 hit  2 surprise  (0%) for a row whose saved record says unmeasurable_surprises: 2. The count is saved but never shown, so the zero still hides it.
• The task adds two optional fields to the parser and a suffix like (0%; 0 unhittable, 2 unmeasurable) to that list.
• Older rows without the fields must print exactly as they do today. Absent fields must stay "not recorded", not become 0.
• Tests will be built from real record lines, not hand-typed values. The task also includes a check that breaking the display turns the new tests red.
• `src/commands_risk.rs is already 6532 lines against a size-gate limit of 6526 in tests/module_size.rs`, so the task says how to handle that.

Task 2 (product, small): the help text should explain the difference between `-p` and `--print`.
• With -p, stdout currently includes the model's own leading and trailing newlines (\nPONG\n\n in my test). --print gives just PONG.
• That difference is deliberate and an existing test pins it, so the task changes only the help text and docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md, plus one test.

